# Runtime state under data/ (account snapshots, holdings, runs/, caches) is NOT versioned.
# NOTE: this must stay `data/*` and NOT `data/`. A directory-level ignore cannot be undone
# by a later `!` re-include (git never descends into an excluded directory), so `data/`
# would silently make the two committed settings files un-addable.
data/*
# The template + example ARE committed on purpose: they document the precedence chain
# (CLI/env > settings.local.json > settings.json > dynamic default) and carry no
# machine-specific paths. See storage.settings_dir_for() and L2.16.
!data/settings.json
!data/settings.local.json.example
# Operator override -- may hold absolute deployment paths and is the write target of
# POST /api/settings. Listed explicitly (after the negations) so no future `!data/*.json`
# style rule can accidentally start tracking it.
data/settings.local.json
